<title>ITALY: INA H1 cons pretax profit rises 30 pct.</title>
<headline>INA H1 cons pretax profit rises 30 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons pretax profit			509.83    vs 390.82</p>
<p>    Total premium income		    3.21 trln vs 3.60 trln</p>
<p>    Total net life premium income	 1.37 trln vs 1.27 trln</p>
<p>    Total net non-life premium income   1.68 trln vs 2.01 trln</p>
<p>    Total net premium income		3.05 trln vs 3.28 trln</p>
<p>Note - Insurer INA said the comparison between the first half and the first half 1995 should take account of the sale of a stake in unit CAMAT to France's AGF which left INA with a holding of 19.9 percent. It attributed falls in premium income in part to the CAMAT sale.</p>
<p>INA said that barring a sudden downturn in market conditions, it expected a &quot;far higher&quot; profit in 1996 than in 1995 and a tax rate of around 50 percent.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
